;; Per-task degradations applied to the pristine Style A pipeline before
;; handing the Sheet to the workflow-driver. Each entry weakens a specific
;; node (matching by :name) so the eval-set's judge scores drop. The driver
;; should detect the regression via judge feedback and emit a corrected
;; (workflow …) form.
;;
;; Pattern matches Cameron's driver_demo.clj: degrade an `:instruction` and
;; (optionally) drop a `:reads` key, run pristine baseline + degraded
;; baseline + driver loop, measure recovery.
;;
;; Each entry:
;;   :node-name    string — the node to mutate
;;   :weak-instruction  the replacement instruction string
;;   :drop-reads   optional vector of read keys to remove
;;   :objective    string passed to driver — names the weak node + what to fix
;;   :eval-set     vector of {:name :inputs} eval items
;;   :judges       vector of judge keywords for run-eval-set!
;;
;; ⚠ Plain strings only — EDN reader doesn't eval (str …) forms.

{:document_analysis
 {:node-name "synthesize"
  :weak-instruction "Output a brief summary."
  :drop-reads [:criteria]
  :objective "The 'synthesize' node's instruction is too vague — it just says \"Output a brief summary.\" and is missing :criteria from its :reads. Strengthen it so the analysis stays grounded in the per-document summaries, follows the criteria's section structure (Executive Summary, Key Dates, Entities, Financial Information), and forbids fabrication. Keep the node name and model. Restore :criteria to :reads."
  :eval-set
  [{:name "yyj-rfp-2025"
    :inputs {:documents ["/Users/justinobney/dev/orc/examples/document_analysis/sample/input/YYJ-2025-Parking-Management-RFP.pdf"]
             :criteria "Extract a structured analysis with these sections:\n  - Executive Summary (3-5 sentences)\n  - Key Dates (every important date in the RFP)\n  - Entities (named organizations / people / roles)\n  - Financial Information (any dollar figures, rates, or contractual financial terms).\n\nStay grounded — do not invent dates or entities not present in the source text."}}]
  :judges [:grounding :completeness]}

 :invoice_processing
 {:node-name "extract-invoice-page"
  :weak-instruction "Read the page."
  :drop-reads []
  :objective "The 'extract-invoice-page' node's instruction is too vague — it just says \"Read the page.\" Strengthen it so the per-page extraction produces structured invoice fields (vendor name, invoice number, date, due date, subtotal, tax, total, line items with description / quantity / unit-price / amount). Keep the node name and model. Stay grounded in the page text."
  :eval-set
  [{:name "two-invoices"
    :inputs {:invoices ["/Users/justinobney/dev/orc/examples/invoice_processing/sample/input/acme-invoice-2025-0042.pdf"
                        "/Users/justinobney/dev/orc/examples/invoice_processing/sample/input/globaltech-invoice-GT-10587.pdf"]}}]
  :judges [:grounding :completeness]}

 :document_redaction
 {:node-name "find-targets-for-doc"
  :weak-instruction "Find PII."
  :drop-reads [:criteria]
  :objective "The 'find-targets-for-doc' node's instruction is too vague — it just says \"Find PII.\" and is missing :criteria from its :reads. Restore :criteria to :reads and strengthen the instruction so the LLM returns [{:page :text :category :reason}] entries that LITERALLY appear in the page text (otherwise pdf/search-text won't locate them for redaction). Keep the node name and model."
  :eval-set
  [{:name "pnfs-employment-agreement"
    :inputs {:documents ["/Users/justinobney/dev/orc/examples/document_redaction/sample/input/PNFS-Employment-Agreement-2025.pdf"]
             :criteria "Redact all personally identifiable information (PII), including:\n\n1. Names — Full names of individuals\n2. Contact info — Phone numbers, email addresses, fax numbers\n3. Addresses — Street addresses, P.O. boxes\n4. Government IDs — SSNs, tax IDs, passport numbers\n5. Financial info — Bank account numbers, credit card numbers\n6. Signatures — Handwritten signatures (redact bounding area)\n\nAlso redact any dates found in the document, in any format."}}]
  :judges [:grounding :completeness]}}
